DranzoRMM agent
===============

This computer has the DranzoRMM endpoint management agent installed. It lets
your IT provider monitor, maintain and support the computer: hardware and
software inventory, software and security updates, scripts and remote support.

What it does and does not do
  * It runs as the ordinary, visible systemd service "dranzormm-agent" (as root).
  * It only makes outbound connections to its management server and only
    executes commands signed by that server.
  * It does not hide itself, does not interfere with antivirus or EDR software,
    and shows a visible indicator whenever a remote session is active.

Useful commands
  Status           sudo dranzo-agent status
                   systemctl status dranzormm-agent
  Enrol            sudo dranzo-agent install --server https://AGENT-SERVER --token dz_enroll_...
  Log              /var/lib/dranzormm/agent.log   (root only)
                   journalctl -u dranzormm-agent

Removing the agent (any administrator of this computer can do this)
  Debian/Ubuntu    sudo apt remove dranzo-agent      (keeps the device identity)
                   sudo apt purge dranzo-agent       (also deletes the device identity)
  RHEL/Fedora      sudo dnf remove dranzo-agent      (deletes the device identity)

  If your IT provider protects the agent with an uninstall code:
                   sudo dranzo-agent uninstall --code XXXX
  and then remove the package as above.

Files
  /usr/bin/dranzo-agent                                   the agent
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/dranzormm-agent.service         packaged service unit
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/dranzormm-agent.service.d/      service settings (drop-in)
  /etc/systemd/system/dranzormm-agent.service             written by "dranzo-agent install"
  /etc/dranzormm/                                         bootstrap configuration (root only)
  /var/lib/dranzormm/                                     device key, certificate, state, log (root only)
